      "side": 1,
      "message": "We will want to make `(WGPU)OptionalBool` a native type like `(WGPU)Bool` so that we can do the same magic to allow implicit conversions from C++ `bool` - see `api.h` and `api_cpp.h` for how it works.\n\nThere are a few differences though:\n- `WGPUBool` is a typedef and not an enum, but I think the same trick will still work with `enum WGPUOptionalBool` and `class wgpu::OptionalBool`.\n- We can have an implicit constructor from `bool` but we can\u0027t have an implicit conversion _to_ `bool` because that doesn\u0027t make sense. We could have one to (and from) `std::optional\u003cbool\u003e` but I\u0027m not sure this would be very useful. We will need to do things like `descriptor-\u003edepthWriteEnabled \u003d\u003d /* true?? */` which could be perhaps best done with `operator\u003d\u003d(bool)`, which allows simply `\u003d\u003d true`. Other alternatives are `\u003d\u003d wgpu::OptionalBool(true)` or define constants so you can do `\u003d\u003d wgpu::OptionalBool::True`.\n\nIt _may_ be fine to do this CL as is for now and then try to solve these problems later, but I think it would be best to try to do it from the beginning. We don\u0027t need to have every convenience override but having it be defined as a class in C++ would help us avoid breaking changes later.\n\n+Loko who set this up for Bool",
